IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026): part sga1, module 2.
-- The Sixth Schedule (section 60(1)): the statement in lieu of prospectus. Part 1 (the matters the statement must state, as the form lists them),
-- Part 2 (the reports to be set out) and Part 3 (provisions applying to Parts 1 and 2).
--
-- The form's layout (the blanks "$ ____", the right-hand column of the table, the signature lines and "Date:") only prescribes the wording of a form and is machinery;
-- what the form requires the statement to STATE is the left-hand column, row by row, and is encoded as the `sch 6 Part 1 matter` below. The rows are numbered here
-- in the order of the rendering; the text numbers none of them. The rendering flattens the two-column table, so some right-hand fragments sit between left-hand rows.
-- The Fifth Schedule (which Part 3 paragraph 3 mentions) is shown repealed (line 28508 to 28510): what it said is not in the sources.

