-- Whether a row is one the statement must state. Rows 5, 30 and 31 carry a condition of their own in the form's words; every other row is unconditional
-- (rows 13 and 26 carry an exception, taken in the next two functions).
@ref sch 6 Part 1 (src:28523-28753)
GIVEN matter IS A `sch 6 Part 1 matter`
      `the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `sch 6 Part 1 row 5 where the share capital is divided into different classes, the voting rights and the rights in respect of capital and dividends of each class` THEN
        (IF `the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares, the right of voting at meetings of the company conferred by, and the rights in respect of capital and dividends attached to, the several classes of shares respectively" -- a failed "if" (marginal reading (a))
    WHEN `sch 6 Part 1 row 30 the rates of the dividends paid in each of the 3 preceding financial years, or since incorporation if shorter` THEN
        (IF `the statement is to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a statement to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company, the following items" -- another statement is not covered (periods ruling (c): a scope limit with no "only")
    WHEN `sch 6 Part 1 row 31 the cases in which no dividends have been paid on any class of shares in any of those years` THEN
        (IF `the statement is to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a statement to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company, the following items" -- another statement is not covered (periods ruling (c): a scope limit with no "only")
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Row 13: the vendors' names and addresses, "except where the contract for the purchase or acquisition was entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended
-- to be carried on by the company or the amount of the purchase money is not material".
@ref sch 6 Part 1 (src:28587-28595)
GIVEN `the contract for the purchase or acquisition was entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended to be carried on by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the purchase money is not material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 1 row 13 the vendor's name and address must be stated` MEANS
    IF    `the contract for the purchase or acquisition was entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended to be carried on by the company`
       OR `the amount of the purchase money is not material`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where the contract for the purchase or acquisition was entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended to be carried on by the company or the amount of the purchase money is not material"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Row 26: "every material contract (other than contracts entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended to be carried on by the company or entered into more than 2 years
-- before the delivery of this statement)". Whether a contract is "material" is the judgment the text leaves open: taken as a fact.
@ref sch 6 Part 1 (src:28653-28659)
GIVEN `the contract is a material contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract was entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended to be carried on by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract was entered into more than 2 years before the delivery of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 1 row 26 the contract must be stated as a material contract` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the contract is a material contract`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every material contract" -- a contract that is not material is not covered
    ELSE (IF    `the contract was entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended to be carried on by the company`
             OR `the contract was entered into more than 2 years before the delivery of the statement`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than contracts entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended to be carried on by the company or entered into more than 2 years before the delivery of this statement)"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- Row 29, the last sentence: "a director or expert is deemed to have an indirect interest in a corporation if he or she has any beneficial interest in shares or debentures of a corporation which has an interest
-- in the promotion of, or in the property proposed to be acquired by the company or if he or she has a beneficial interest in shares or debentures in a corporation which is by virtue of section 6 of the Act
-- deemed to be related to that firstmentioned corporation".
@ref sch 6 Part 1 (src:28682-28736)
GIVEN `the director or expert has a beneficial interest in shares or debentures of a corporation which has an interest in the promotion of, or in the property proposed to be acquired by, the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director or expert has a beneficial interest in shares or debentures in a corporation which is by virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to that firstmentioned corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 1 row 29 the director or expert is deemed to have an indirect interest in the corporation` MEANS
    IF    `the director or expert has a beneficial interest in shares or debentures of a corporation which has an interest in the promotion of, or in the property proposed to be acquired by, the company`
       OR `the director or expert has a beneficial interest in shares or debentures in a corporation which is by virtue of section 6 deemed to be related to that firstmentioned corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a director or expert is deemed to have an indirect interest in a corporation if he or she has any beneficial interest in shares or debentures of a corporation which has an interest in the promotion of, or in the property proposed to be acquired by the company or if he or she has a beneficial interest in shares or debentures in a corporation which is by virtue of section 6 of the Act deemed to be related to that firstmentioned corporation" -- a failed "if" in a deeming (marginal reading (a))

-- Whether the statement states every matter that must be stated: each row the form requires (JUST TRUE above) is among the matters the statement states.
-- A row whose requirement is NOTHING is not required on those facts, and a row that is JUST FALSE is not required either.
@ref sch 6 Part 1 (src:28523-28753)
GIVEN `the matters the statement states` IS A LIST OF `sch 6 Part 1 matter`
      `the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` MEANS
    all (GIVEN m YIELD (IF `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` m `the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares` `the statement is to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                        THEN elem m `the matters the statement states`
                        ELSE TRUE)) `sch 6 Part 1 all the rows of the form`

§ `Sixth Schedule, Part 2: the reports to be set out`

§§ `Part 2 paragraph 1: the acquisition of a business or limited liability partnership`

-- 1. Where it is proposed to acquire a business or limited liability partnership, a report by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company (who must be named in the statement)
-- with respect to (a) the profits or losses of the business or partnership in respect of each of the 3 financial years immediately preceding the lodging of the statement with the Registrar;
-- and (b) the assets and liabilities at the last date to which its accounts were made up.
-- src:28766 | 1. Where it is proposed to acquire a business or limited liability partnership, a
-- src:28767 | report by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company (who must be
-- src:28768 | named in the statement) with respect to —
-- src:28770 | (a) the profits or losses of the business or limited liability partnership in
-- src:28771 | respect of each of the 3 financial years immediately preceding the
-- src:28772 | lodging of the statement with the Registrar; and
-- src:28774 | (b) the assets and liabilities of the business or limited liability partnership
-- src:28775 | at the last date to which the accounts of the business or limited liability
-- src:28776 | partnership were made up.
@ref sch 6 Part 2 para 1 (src:28766-28776)
GIVEN `it is proposed to acquire a business or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 2 para 1 a report is required` MEANS
    IF `it is proposed to acquire a business or limited liability partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is proposed to acquire a business or limited liability partnership, a report by a public accountant" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a))

@ref sch 6 Part 2 para 1 (src:28766-28776)
GIVEN `the report is by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public accountant is named in the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of financial years immediately preceding the lodging of the statement for which the report gives the profits or losses` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of financial years the paragraph requires, after Part 3 paragraph 4` IS A NUMBER
      `the report gives the assets and liabilities at the last date to which the accounts were made up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 2 para 1 the report has the content the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the report is by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company`
      AND `the public accountant is named in the statement`
      AND `the number of financial years immediately preceding the lodging of the statement for which the report gives the profits or losses` AT LEAST `the number of financial years the paragraph requires, after Part 3 paragraph 4`
      AND `the report gives the assets and liabilities at the last date to which the accounts were made up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a report by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company (who must be named in the statement) with respect to -- (a) the profits or losses ... in respect of each of the 3 financial years immediately preceding the lodging of the statement with the Registrar; and (b) the assets and liabilities ... at the last date to which the accounts ... were made up" (a duty not met, the paragraph's own question)

§§ `Part 2 paragraph 2: the acquisition of shares in a corporation that becomes a subsidiary`

-- 2.-(1) Where it is proposed to acquire shares in a corporation which by reason of the acquisition or anything to be done in consequence or in connection with it will become a subsidiary of the company,
-- a report by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company (who must be named in the statement) with respect to the profits and losses and assets and liabilities of the other corporation in accordance
-- with sub-paragraph (2) or (3), indicating how the profits and losses would, in respect of the shares to be acquired, have concerned members of the company, and what allowance would have fallen to be made, in
-- relation to assets and liabilities, for holders of other shares, if the company had at all material times held the shares to be acquired.
-- src:28778 | 2.—(1) Where it is proposed to acquire shares in a corporation which by reason
-- src:28779 | of the acquisition or anything to be done in consequence thereof or in connection
-- src:28780 | therewith will become a subsidiary of the company, a report by a public
-- src:28781 | accountant appointed as auditor of the company (who must be named in the
-- src:28782 | statement) with respect to the profits and losses and assets and liabilities of the
-- src:28783 | other corporation in accordance with sub‑paragraph (2) or (3) (as the case
-- src:28784 | requires) indicating how the profits and losses of the other corporation dealt with
-- src:28785 | by the report would, in respect of the shares to be acquired, have concerned
-- src:28786 | members of the company, and what allowance would have fallen to be made, in
-- src:28787 | relation to assets and liabilities so dealt with, for holders of other shares, if the
-- src:28788 | company had at all material times held the shares to be acquired.
@ref sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) (src:28778-28788)
GIVEN `it is proposed to acquire shares in a corporation which by reason of the acquisition or anything to be done in consequence or in connection with it will become a subsidiary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) a report is required` MEANS
    IF `it is proposed to acquire shares in a corporation which by reason of the acquisition or anything to be done in consequence or in connection with it will become a subsidiary of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is proposed to acquire shares in a corporation which by reason of the acquisition or anything to be done in consequence thereof or in connection therewith will become a subsidiary of the company, a report" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a))

@ref sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) (src:28778-28788)
GIVEN `the report is by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public accountant is named in the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report deals with the other corporation in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) or (3), as the case requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report indicates how the profits and losses of the other corporation would, in respect of the shares to be acquired, have concerned members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report indicates what allowance would have fallen to be made, in relation to assets and liabilities, for holders of other shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) the report has the content the sub-paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the report is by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company`
      AND `the public accountant is named in the statement`
      AND `the report deals with the other corporation in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) or (3), as the case requires`
      AND `the report indicates how the profits and losses of the other corporation would, in respect of the shares to be acquired, have concerned members of the company`
      AND `the report indicates what allowance would have fallen to be made, in relation to assets and liabilities, for holders of other shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a report by a public accountant appointed as auditor of the company (who must be named in the statement) with respect to the profits and losses and assets and liabilities of the other corporation in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) or (3) (as the case requires) indicating how the profits and losses ... would, in respect of the shares to be acquired, have concerned members of the company, and what allowance would have fallen to be made, in relation to assets and liabilities so dealt with, for holders of other shares" (a duty not met, the paragraph's own question)

-- (2) If the other corporation has no subsidiaries, the report must (a) so far as regards profits and losses, deal with the profits or losses of the other corporation in respect of each of the 3 financial years
-- immediately preceding the delivery of the statement to the Registrar; and (b) so far as regards assets and liabilities, deal with them at the last date to which the accounts were made up.
-- src:28790 | (2) If the other corporation has no subsidiaries, the report mentioned in
-- src:28791 | sub‑paragraph (1) must —
-- src:28793 | (a) so far as regards profits and losses — deal with the profits or losses of
-- src:28794 | the other corporation in respect of each of the 3 financial years
-- src:28795 | immediately preceding the delivery of the statement to the Registrar;
-- src:28796 | and
-- src:28798 | (b) so far as regards assets and liabilities — deal with the assets and
-- src:28799 | liabilities of the other corporation at the last date to which the accounts
-- src:28800 | of the corporation were made up.
@ref sch 6 Part 2 para 2(2) (src:28790-28800)
GIVEN `the other corporation has no subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of financial years immediately preceding the delivery of the statement for which the report deals with the profits or losses of the other corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of financial years the paragraph requires, after Part 3 paragraph 4` IS A NUMBER
      `the report deals with the assets and liabilities of the other corporation at the last date to which its accounts were made up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 2 para 2(2) the report deals with the other corporation as the sub-paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the other corporation has no subsidiaries`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the other corporation has no subsidiaries, the report mentioned in sub-paragraph (1) must" -- a failed "if": sub-paragraph (2) does not apply to a corporation that has subsidiaries (marginal reading (a))
    ELSE (IF    `the number of financial years immediately preceding the delivery of the statement for which the report deals with the profits or losses of the other corporation` AT LEAST `the number of financial years the paragraph requires, after Part 3 paragraph 4`
              AND `the report deals with the assets and liabilities of the other corporation at the last date to which its accounts were made up`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the report mentioned in sub-paragraph (1) must -- (a) so far as regards profits and losses -- deal with the profits or losses of the other corporation in respect of each of the 3 financial years immediately preceding the delivery of the statement to the Registrar; and (b) so far as regards assets and liabilities -- deal with the assets and liabilities of the other corporation at the last date to which the accounts of the corporation were made up" (a duty not met)

-- (3) If the other corporation has subsidiaries, the report must (a) so far as regards profits and losses, deal separately with the other corporation's own as (2) provides and, in addition, deal either (i) as a whole with
-- the combined profits or losses of its subsidiaries or (ii) individually with those of each subsidiary, or, instead of dealing separately, deal as a whole with the profits or losses of the other corporation and with the
-- combined profits or losses of its subsidiaries; and (b) so far as regards assets and liabilities, deal separately with the other corporation's as (2) provides and, in addition, deal either (i) as a whole with the combined
-- assets and liabilities of its subsidiaries, with or without the other corporation's, or (ii) individually with each subsidiary; and must indicate, as respects the profits or losses and the assets and liabilities of the
-- subsidiaries, the allowance to be made for persons other than members of the company.
-- src:28802 | (3) If the other corporation has subsidiaries, the report mentioned in
-- src:28803 | sub‑paragraph (1) must —
-- src:28805 | (a) so far as regards profits and losses — deal separately with the other
-- src:28806 | corporation’s profits or losses as provided by sub‑paragraph (2), and,
-- src:28807 | in addition, deal as aforesaid either —
-- src:28814 | (i) as a whole — with the combined profits or losses of its
-- src:28815 | subsidiaries; or
-- src:28817 | (ii) individually — with the profits or losses of each subsidiary,
-- src:28819 | (a) or, instead of dealing separately with the other corporation’s profits or
-- src:28820 | losses, deal as aforesaid as a whole with the profits or losses of the
-- src:28821 | other corporation and with the combined profits or losses of its
-- src:28822 | subsidiaries; and
-- src:28824 | (b) so far as regards assets and liabilities — deal separately with the other
-- src:28825 | corporation’s assets and liabilities as provided by sub‑paragraph (2),
-- src:28826 | and, in addition, deal as aforesaid either —
-- src:28828 | (i) as a whole — with the combined assets and liabilities of its
-- src:28829 | subsidiaries, with or without the other corporation’s assets and
-- src:28830 | liabilities; or
-- src:28832 | (ii) individually — with the assets and liabilities of each
-- src:28833 | subsidiary,
-- src:28835 | (b) and must indicate as respects the profits or losses and the assets and
-- src:28836 | liabilities of the subsidiaries the allowance to be made for persons
-- src:28837 | other than members of the company.
@ref sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3) (src:28802-28837)
GIVEN `the other corporation has subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report deals separately with the other corporation's profits or losses as sub-paragraph (2) provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report deals with the combined profits or losses of the subsidiaries as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report deals with the profits or losses of each subsidiary individually` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report deals as a whole with the profits or losses of the other corporation and with the combined profits or losses of its subsidiaries, instead of dealing separately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(a) the report deals with profits and losses as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the other corporation has subsidiaries`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the other corporation has subsidiaries, the report mentioned in sub-paragraph (1) must" -- a failed "if": sub-paragraph (3) does not apply to a corporation that has no subsidiaries (marginal reading (a))
    ELSE (IF    (    `the report deals separately with the other corporation's profits or losses as sub-paragraph (2) provides`
                 AND (`the report deals with the combined profits or losses of the subsidiaries as a whole` OR `the report deals with the profits or losses of each subsidiary individually`))
             OR `the report deals as a whole with the profits or losses of the other corporation and with the combined profits or losses of its subsidiaries, instead of dealing separately`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) so far as regards profits and losses -- deal separately with the other corporation's profits or losses as provided by sub-paragraph (2), and, in addition, deal as aforesaid either -- (i) as a whole -- with the combined profits or losses of its subsidiaries; or (ii) individually -- with the profits or losses of each subsidiary, -- (a) or, instead of dealing separately with the other corporation's profits or losses, deal as aforesaid as a whole with the profits or losses of the other corporation and with the combined profits or losses of its subsidiaries" (a duty not met)

@ref sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3) (src:28802-28837)
GIVEN `the other corporation has subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report deals separately with the other corporation's assets and liabilities as sub-paragraph (2) provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report deals with the combined assets and liabilities of the subsidiaries as a whole, with or without the other corporation's assets and liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report deals with the assets and liabilities of each subsidiary individually` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(b) the report deals with assets and liabilities as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the other corporation has subsidiaries`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the other corporation has subsidiaries, the report mentioned in sub-paragraph (1) must" -- a failed "if": sub-paragraph (3) does not apply to a corporation that has no subsidiaries (marginal reading (a))
    ELSE (IF    `the report deals separately with the other corporation's assets and liabilities as sub-paragraph (2) provides`
            AND (`the report deals with the combined assets and liabilities of the subsidiaries as a whole, with or without the other corporation's assets and liabilities` OR `the report deals with the assets and liabilities of each subsidiary individually`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) so far as regards assets and liabilities -- deal separately with the other corporation's assets and liabilities as provided by sub-paragraph (2), and, in addition, deal as aforesaid either -- (i) as a whole -- with the combined assets and liabilities of its subsidiaries, with or without the other corporation's assets and liabilities; or (ii) individually -- with the assets and liabilities of each subsidiary" (a duty not met)

@ref sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3) (src:28802-28837)
GIVEN `the report indicates, as respects the profits or losses and the assets and liabilities of the subsidiaries, the allowance to be made for persons other than members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3) the report indicates the allowance for persons other than members of the company` MEANS
    IF `the report indicates, as respects the profits or losses and the assets and liabilities of the subsidiaries, the allowance to be made for persons other than members of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and must indicate as respects the profits or losses and the assets and liabilities of the subsidiaries the allowance to be made for persons other than members of the company" (a duty not met)

