§ `Sixth Schedule, Part 3: provisions applying to Parts 1 and 2`

-- 3. In this Schedule "vendor" includes any person who is a vendor for the purposes of the repealed Fifth Schedule, and "financial year" has the meaning assigned to it in Part 3 of that Schedule.
-- "vendor": an "includes" term, so a person who is not a vendor for the purposes of the Fifth Schedule is not thereby excluded (NOTHING). "financial year": handed to a repealed Schedule not in the sources:
-- the fact that the Fifth Schedule's meaning is met is asked.
-- src:28853 | 3. In this Schedule “vendor” includes any person who is a vendor for the
-- src:28854 | purposes of the repealed Fifth Schedule, and “financial year” has the meaning
-- src:28855 | assigned to it in Part 3 of that Schedule.
@ref sch 6 Part 3 para 3 (src:28853-28855)
GIVEN `the person is a vendor for the purposes of the repealed Fifth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 3 para 3 "vendor" the person is within the word vendor` MEANS
    IF `the person is a vendor for the purposes of the repealed Fifth Schedule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): ""vendor" includes any person who is a vendor for the purposes of the repealed Fifth Schedule" -- the list is open

@ref sch 6 Part 3 para 3 (src:28853-28855)
GIVEN `the period is a financial year as Part 3 of the repealed Fifth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 3 para 3 "financial year" the period is a financial year` MEANS
    IF `the period is a financial year as Part 3 of the repealed Fifth Schedule gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""financial year" has the meaning assigned to it in Part 3 of that Schedule" -- a definition handed to another source (the repealed Fifth Schedule is not in the sources, so its test is asked as a fact: delegated-definitions ruling (a))

-- Part 3 paragraph 4: for a business, corporation or partnership that has carried on business for less than 3 years and whose accounts were made up for 2 years or one year only, Part 2 has effect as if
-- 2 years or one year were substituted for 3 years. The answer is the number of financial years a report must deal with.
-- src:28857 | 4. If, in the case of a business which has been carried on or of a corporation or
-- src:28858 | limited liability partnership which has been carrying on business for less than
-- src:28859 | 3 years, the accounts of the business or corporation or limited liability partnership
-- src:28860 | have only been made up in respect of 2 years or one year, Part 2 of this Schedule
-- src:28861 | has effect as if references to 2 years or one year (as the case may be) were
-- src:28862 | substituted for references to 3 years.
@ref sch 6 Part 3 para 4 (src:28857-28862)
GIVEN `the business, corporation or limited liability partnership has been carrying on business for less than 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of years for which its accounts have been made up` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 6 Part 3 para 4 the number of financial years a report must deal with` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the business, corporation or limited liability partnership has been carrying on business for less than 3 years`)
    THEN JUST 3
    ELSE (IF `the number of years for which its accounts have been made up` EQUALS 2
          THEN JUST 2
          ELSE (IF `the number of years for which its accounts have been made up` EQUALS 1
                THEN JUST 1
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the accounts ... have only been made up in respect of 2 years or one year" -- no accounts at all, or accounts for 3 years, are outside the paragraph

-- 5. Any report required by Part 2 must either indicate by way of note any adjustments to the figures that appear to the persons making the report necessary, or must make those adjustments and
-- indicate that adjustments have been made.
-- src:28869 | 5. Any report required by Part 2 of this Schedule must either indicate by way of
-- src:28870 | note any adjustments as respects the figures of any profits or losses or assets and
-- src:28871 | liabilities dealt with by the report which appear to the persons making the report
-- src:28872 | necessary or must make those adjustments and indicate that adjustments have
-- src:28873 | been made.
@ref sch 6 Part 3 para 5 (src:28869-28873)
GIVEN `the report indicates by way of note the adjustments that appear to the persons making it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report makes those adjustments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report indicates that adjustments have been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 Part 3 para 5 the report deals with adjustments as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the report indicates by way of note the adjustments that appear to the persons making it necessary`
       OR (`the report makes those adjustments` AND `the report indicates that adjustments have been made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any report required by Part 2 of this Schedule must either indicate by way of note any adjustments ... or must make those adjustments and indicate that adjustments have been made" (a duty not met, the paragraph's own question)
